silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_05_cannon_or_gpt_absorption_decomposition_step__step_sous_position a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The sous position is the under-reading observation role in the local olog. It is not a deployed service, not a narrator, not a replacement for the governed apex. It reads the incoming profile Hom(-, MittensColimitApex) and the outgoing profile Hom(MittensColimitApex, -) and reports missing or forbidden arrows." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_05_cannon_or_gpt_absorption_decomposition_step__step_y_inx_=_homx__mittens;_y_outx_=_hommittens__x a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Y_in(X) is the incoming Hom-set: the set of all typed arrows from X to MittensColimitApex. Y_out(X) is the outgoing Hom-set: the set of all typed arrows from MittensColimitApex to X. Together they define the representable profile of Mittens-the-cat in the local olog." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_05_cannon_or_gpt_absorption_decomposition_step__step_yoneda_lemma_joc_§6_18_6_20 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The Yoneda lemma (JoC §6.18-6.20): Nat(Hom(-,A), F) ≅ F(A) naturally. The representable profile Hom(-,A) fully determines A up to isomorphism; an object is known by its incoming arrows. For Mittens: the twelve typed legs in Y_in(A) for A ranging over D_Mittens sources fully determine MittensColimitApex." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_05_cannon_or_gpt_absorption_decomposition_step__step_cannon_gpt_absorption_route a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "A cannon text (e.g. the ITIS taxonomy database entry for Felis catus TSN 183798) contributes typed vocabulary. Before it becomes an olog leg for the Mittens cocone, it must pass the Node-or-Arrow gate: it must be assigned a typed source node (FelisCatusTSN183798), a typed arrow (taxonomy_leg), and a cocone-compatibility check. Only after gate passage does it become an olog leg." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_05_cannon_or_gpt_absorption_decomposition_step__step_yoneda_inheritance_of_sous_law a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By Yoneda naturality, the sous observation law transports to every downstream paper: any paper that uses 'sous', 'cannon', or 'GPT absorption' must answer 'what is sous here' before operational use, define the incoming and outgoing profile pair, and show the Node-or-Arrow gate passage for every absorbed source." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_05_cannon_or_gpt_absorption_decomposition_step__step_sous_yoneda_law_recap a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Sous is the under-reading observation role; Y_in(X) = Hom(X, Mittens) and Y_out(X) = Hom(Mittens, X) are the dual profiles; the Yoneda lemma makes the profile the fingerprint; cannon and GPT material must pass the Node-or-Arrow gate before becoming olog legs; the sous law is inherited by all 41 sibling papers." .
